    {
      "type": "post",
      "id": "7467643115722690562",
      "entityId": "7467643115722690562",
      "linkedinUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/sarahbarneshumphrey_somewhere-on-your-phone-theres-a-note-a-activity-7467643115722690562-fjwi",
      "shareLinkedinUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:share:7467643114653024256",
      "shareUrn": "urn:li:share:7467643114653024256",
      "content": "Somewhere on your phone there's a note, a voice memo, a half-written plan for something you keep meaning to start.\n\n(Or maybe that's just me.)\n\nIt's the start of a new month, so you think, \"Okay, this time I'll actually do it.\"\n\nBut you don't.\n\nBecause maybe your plan isn't perfect yet. Or you don't feel 100% ready. Or the timing doesn't make sense.\n\nHere's what I've learned after years of building, failing, and rebuilding ...\n\nThe gap between where you are and where you want to be has nothing to do with your 'talent' or 'timing.'\n\n***It's the start you keep postponing***\n\nYou're NEVER going to feel ready.\n\nWhy? Because that feeling doesn't come before you start - it comes after.\n\nSo start messy. Start scared. Start anyway. Just start.\n\n---\n\nThere's less than 30 days left in Q2. What's one thing you've been putting off that you're going to start?\n\nI want to hear 👇🏻",
