    {
      "type": "post",
      "id": "7477405710973321217",
      "entityId": "7477405710973321217",
      "linkedinUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/sarahbarneshumphrey_samsarabeyond2026-activity-7477405710973321217-mhlX",
      "shareLinkedinUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:ugcPost:7477405709954023425",
      "shareUrn": "urn:li:ugcPost:7477405709954023425",
      "content": "Supply chain doesn't work without drivers.\n\nI was at Samsara Beyond in Las Vegas last week, and I got to record four podcast episodes while I was there.\n\nOne thing that kept coming up in almost every conversation?\n\nThe next generation isn't opposed to driving.\nThey're opposed to outdated cabs.\n\nWhen the technology inside the truck matches what they use in their everyday lives, driving becomes a job they (actually) want. \n\nWhen it doesn't? We lose them before we ever have them.\n\nBottom line: we're not going to be able to recruit our way out of the driver shortage.\n\nWe're going to have to BUILD our way out of it.\n\nAnd that starts with investing in what's happening INSIDE the cab.\n\nWho else attended #SamsaraBeyond2026? I'm curious what you took away.",
