      "content": "I recently heard about a data issue FedEx had 📦 \n\nNot the kind that waves a red flag. The kind that quietly starts costing you money.\n\nGOAT Group uses FedEx to ship hundreds of thousands of packages a month. So at that volume, a \"small\" problem isn't small for long.\n\nThey caught it fast because they had Reveel's platform watching for anything that looked off.\n\nAnd instead of spending weeks figuring out what went wrong, they went straight to fixing it.\n\nThat's the part that stuck with me.\n\n**Most teams are looking at what their data shows them. Not what their data is hiding.**\n\nGabrielle Murabito and Gloria Seckler shared that story with me at Home Delivery World. \n\nTwo women leading some of the sharpest data conversations in this space, which I love to see.\n\nOur conversation is now on the Let's Talk Supply Chain pod and it's worth the listen: https://lnkd.in/eCCgZETE",
